From: godotjs
Subject: [godotjs] abseil: link CoreFoundation on the iOS build as well

Anything that links abseil needs CoreFoundation: absl::time_internal::local_time_zone
calls CFTimeZoneCopyDefault, CFStringGetCString and friends. The only place that
framework was named is xcode_settings.OTHER_LDFLAGS, and gyp's ninja generator turns
xcode_settings into flags for the mac flavour only (`if self.flavor == "mac"` in
tools/gyp/pylib/gyp/generator/ninja.py). With --dest-os=ios the flavour is ios, so
the framework was never passed and the first binary to link abseil stopped:

  Undefined symbols for architecture arm64:
    "_CFTimeZoneCopyDefault", referenced from:
        absl::time_internal::cctz::local_time_zone() in libabseil.a[108](...)

List the framework the way every flavour reads it (`libraries`), for both spellings
of an Apple host: the iOS build's host tools - torque is the first one linked - are
macOS executables, and depending on the toolset they report the host OS or the
destination OS. Naming a framework twice on a link line is the same framework, so
macOS builds only repeat what xcode_settings already added.
diff --git a/tools/v8_gypfiles/abseil.gyp b/tools/v8_gypfiles/abseil.gyp
index 1a1de33..acc05fa 100644
--- a/tools/v8_gypfiles/abseil.gyp
+++ b/tools/v8_gypfiles/abseil.gyp
@@ -15,6 +15,25 @@
         'xcode_settings': {
           'OTHER_LDFLAGS': ['-framework CoreFoundation'],
         },
+        # Linking abseil needs CoreFoundation (absl::time_internal::cctz::local_time_zone
+        # calls CFTimeZoneCopyDefault and friends). The xcode_settings line above only
+        # reaches the linker for the mac flavour, so an iOS build stopped with
+        # "Undefined symbols: _CFTimeZoneCopyDefault, _CFStringGetCString, ...".
+        # Both spellings are listed on purpose: the iOS build's host tools (torque
+        # first) are macOS executables and may report the host OS or the destination
+        # OS depending on the toolset, and a framework named twice on a link line is
+        # the same framework. macOS command lines only gain a repeat of what
+        # xcode_settings already added.
+        'conditions': [
+          [ 'OS in "mac ios"', {
+            'libraries': [ '-framework CoreFoundation' ],
+          }],
+        ],
+        'conditions': [
+          [ 'OS=="ios"', {
+            'libraries': [ '-framework CoreFoundation' ],
+          }],
+        ],
       },
       'include_dirs': [
         '<(ABSEIL_ROOT)',
